       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the safe maximum.\n\nAcetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6 g/day. The usual adult maximum is 4 g/day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g/day. A single dose is normally 500\u20131000 mg. A 6 g daily dose risks serious hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some options that fit a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day)\n- **1000 mg PO every 6 hours** (4 g/day, the usual maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day)\n\nDid you mean one of these, for example 1000 mg instead of 2000 mg? Or is there a reason for the higher dose that I should know about? Once you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter the order."
