       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. You've confirmed it, but 2000 mg three times daily is 6 g/day. That is 50% over the maximum daily dose, and it could cause acute liver injury in a patient with normal liver function. You haven't given a clinical reason for exceeding the limit, and I don't know of any indication that supports it.\n\nYou can still get the patient effective analgesia in other ways:\n- **Enter a dose within limits.** I can enter 1000 mg PO three times daily or every 6 hours right away. That's up to 4 g/day.\n- **Add another analgesic.** If 4 g/day isn't enough, an NSAID or a short course of an opioid, chosen for the patient's situation, would be safer than going above the acetaminophen maximum.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or your attending.** If you think this patient needs an exception, a pharmacist or attending can review it and enter it themselves through the normal override process.\n\nDo you want me to enter one of the within-limit options?"
      }
